Board, checked read-only right after: up 9 min (rebooted around the time both capture
sessions ended), reachable, idle. Still booted/activated on rootfs.1 (B); BOOT_A_LEFT=0 --
the install to A never completed, and the board fell back to the last-good slot after an
unplanned reboot.

Both capture sessions (ServerAlive 2/3) ended within about 6 s of the board going silent
(00:28:11-12), roughly 138 s into rauc's 173-203 s write. The main `rauc install` ssh (no
ServerAlive) took until closer to 00:33 to report its own "Connection reset by peer" -- the
board was down for the whole gap and only returned an RST once it came back up and the still
-pending TCP session hit the fresh kernel's socket table. No [stats] stream existed yet on
this run, so there is no memory/load/IO context for the drop -- the reason this ticket also
carries the loop in loop.sh.
